WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:10.740
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, you guys submitted
a lot of good questions for my Episode 2 Q&amp;A.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.911
I’m almost done moving too so eventually
this will all look like I’m not making these

00:00:16.911 --> 00:00:18.450
videos from limbo or something.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.190
You guys picked up on a lot of good easter
eggs I missed.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.700
And lots of good Missy and Danny Pink theories.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.590
Let’s get in it, careful for spoilers from
the episode if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.180
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.110
1 - Action vids asks Why didn’t the Dalek
recognize the Doctor?

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.110
All because of the regeneration.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.660
His memory banks only went up to Matt Smith.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.420
There was a little confusion because of souffle
girl Clara erasing the doctor from their collective

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.530
memory and then the Daleks re-learning about
him in the christmas special after assimilating

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.710
Tasha Lem.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.489
The Daleks have independent minds, the khaled
mutants do.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:52.469
But they also have the machine parts with
data banks that record and distribute new

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:54.239
memories each individual dalek picks up.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:59.010
Rusty rejoined the Dalek Fleet at the end
of the episode so it’s possible he withheld

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.570
new information about the Doctor.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.280
I think they’ll follow up on it at some
point.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.479
2 - Walking Who asks What do you think of
Danny Pink’s Story so far?

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:15.190
I like him a lot, we haven’t gotten a long
Danny Pink episode yet, so I’m withholding

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.540
a lot of comments till then.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:22.430
There were pictures from the set of people
connected to him.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:29.729
I think Episode 4 is supposed to add a lot
of backstory.

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:33.299
Like I said in my review, Samuel Anderson
does a good job of going from funny to dark

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:37.409
in a heartbeat, he’s not quite as grand
as Capaldi but I think being able to turn

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:42.549
on a dime like that is really important for
Doctor Who stories.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:47.530
As far as new characters go I think he’s
an interesting new flavor, there are going

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.189
to be a few more new characters we haven’t
met yet.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:55.060
I think they did a great job casting them
all so whatever their stories are I’m sure

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.789
they’ll be interesting and fun.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:03.479
3 - Tigerblood asks Do you think "Rusty" will
be a returning character?

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:08.380
Definitely, it felt like Moffat created something
so unusual in this “good” dalek that it

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.039
would be a complete waste to not use the opportunity
to throw a wrinkle into all future Capaldi

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:12.039
Dalek stories.

00:02:12.039 --> 00:02:13.039
Rusty is the new Handles.

00:02:13.039 --> 00:02:17.180
What I’d really like to see is a Rusty scene
several episodes down the road where he comes

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.790
back with his own armada.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:22.510
Like Rusty has started converting other Daleks
to his cause bit by bit.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.360
Then rides in like the cavalry to help the
Doctor in a moment of need.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.410
I think it will have something to do with
the Missy plot, when it comes to whatever

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.659
the final conflict is in the finale.

00:02:32.659 --> 00:02:36.640
I’m always a fan of enemies working together
as friends for a brief period.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.250
And the Daleks are the Time Lords greatest
enemies.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.650
Unless you consider the Time Lords to be their
own worst enemies.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:48.470
4 - Davijoman asks Do you think that Missy
will snag everyone that dies in all the episodes?

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.810
So that they all can appear with her in the
finale.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:57.849
She has shown up in consecutive episodes so
it does seem that way.

00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:03.970
I do think the circumstances of a person’s
death is important to being snatched.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.689
It’s still a bit unclear as to what part
of each person she’s snatching.

00:03:08.689 --> 00:03:13.230
Life Force, full on teleportation at the moment
of death or if it’s a Silence in the Library

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:16.420
situation, where copies are made of people.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.159
It seems pretty clear that she wants to win
people over with very sinister kindness and

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:25.799
going so far as to call her domain Heaven
be it TARDIS or be it Pocket Universe, makes

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:31.590
it sound like she’s got plans for the Doctor
that require all those people.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:37.490
If she wanted to kill him she wouldn’t have
called him her boyfriend and she wouldn’t

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.010
have said she’d keep the scottish accent.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.489
So the question we need to ask is, what does
she want to help the doctor do that requires

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:45.489
an army?

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:47.280
I’ve spent a lot of time talking about Series
8 and broken promises.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.510
But what if Missy is collecting people as
a way of fulfilling a promise to the Doctor.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:56.421
It would be an interesting twist if everyone
the doctor considered close to him broke his

00:03:56.421 --> 00:03:59.900
trust, but the sinister person was the only
one who didn’t break a promise.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.390
Then there’s the question of what that promise
might be.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:06.879
I love how Capaldi’s doctor has so many
questions and works everything out by lecturing

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:11.810
to himself using a chalkboard.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.040
That should be his catchphrase, just “Question?”

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.350
5 - Benjamin asks, if Heaven is like the TARDIS
then shouldn’t the dead soldier have been

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.940
tiny when she woke up?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.060
Very interesting, yes.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.759
Missy’s garden does look a lot like a TARDIS
console.

00:04:24.759 --> 00:04:28.030
If it is, you would think they’d still be
small after she materialized it around them.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.840
I think it’s more evidence that she’s
only saving parts of people.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.440
It’s still unclear whether it’s just their
consciousness.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.190
Like a Silence in the Library situation or
if it’s their soul or life force.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.400
Those are things we’ll need more missy scenes
to figure out.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.919
Right now she’s only been on screen for
a few moments.

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:46.500
All that is clear is that she is very similar
to the Doctor and they have a history together.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.759
6 - Alex asks do you think Danny Pink would
leave the show if Clara left or would he stay

00:04:50.759 --> 00:04:52.550
as a companion?

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.789
I think he would stay, someone in the comments
said Samuel Anderson claimed he wasn’t a

00:04:53.789 --> 00:04:54.789
companion in an interview but it could just
be misdirection.

00:04:54.789 --> 00:04:56.190
The Doctor will not travel for a whole series
without a companion.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.910
There might be episodes where we don’t see
companions, but the foundation of the show

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:58.910
is that The Doctor travels with someone or
something.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.639
It wouldn’t be doctor who if he didn’t
have someone besides himself to listen to

00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:02.639
him.

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:09.490
If Jenna and Samuel Anderson are both leaving
by the christmas special I think we’d also

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.710
see a teaser for who the next official companion
is in that episode.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:17.410
So regardless of what happens, all questions
will be answered by the special.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.970
We still don’t even know what the title
is, last year they didn’t shoot Matt Smith’s

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.970
christmas special till around this time in
the year.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:27.240
So we might get some new info over the next
several weeks.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.830
7 - Sandrine asks Do you think that the missy
situation will trigger darker instincts in

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.110
the Doctor like the Time Lord Victorious moments?

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:38.520
I think it would be really cool if the Missy
plot became a huge callback to the moment

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.530
in episode 1 where the robot asked, do you
have it in you to kill me doctor?

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.060
Like Missy will force the Doctor to kill her.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.280
That would be as dark as the show could go.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.380
All of episode 2 was about the Doctor showing
himself to be a good Dalek.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:58.139
He’s going to continue to wrestle with his
dark passenger.

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:01.160
For those that watched Dexter.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:08.020
I think Doctor Who as a series will always
end things on a note of closure even if we’re

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.020
crying during the finale.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:14.150
So I don’t think the Doctor would completely
trash his motto.

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:16.000
“Never cruel or cowardly.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.780
Never give up, never give in.”

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:21.280
I think killing Missy would be the cowardly
act.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:26.630
8 - cajun asks Will Souffle Girl Clara turning
into a Dalek be important to anything going

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.990
on in series 8?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:36.349
I think the Impossible Girl persona will be
referenced, but I don’t think that specific

00:06:36.349 --> 00:06:38.660
version of Clara will play a critical role.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.720
Regardless of which Clara explanation you
believe, like which version of Clara she is

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.320
right now, be it a copy or the original.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.340
I think that’s pretty much done with.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.380
I think all future references to multiple
claras will be jokes or subtle references

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.270
the characters make, like clara making fun
of herself.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.680
I don’t think it’s going to play a huge
role in the missy storyline.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.319
Keep your eyes peeled for references the other
claras, but I think they’ll just be that,

00:06:57.319 --> 00:06:58.639
winks to series 7b.

00:06:58.639 --> 00:07:02.400
9 - Dova Kain asks, when the doctor healed
Rusty and we saw the crack in the wall was

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.500
the root cause, did it have anything to do
with the timelords?

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.470
I think that was a visual reminder about the
time lords, but I don’t think the time lords

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.350
or the real cracks in the universe had anything
to do with Rusty.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:17.169
When the doctor was showing him his memories
there were a lot of flashbacks to different

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.410
moments in doctor who history.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:22.479
But I don’t think the physical cracks in
the universe were there to purposefully alter

00:07:22.479 --> 00:07:23.479
rusty.

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:25.509
If the time lords wanted to contact the doctor
again, they probably would have done it in

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:27.220
a more direct way.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:33.040
I think Rusty was an anomaly that the doctor
just seized on.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:38.881
I know Moffat also writes Sherlock and on
that show, Benedict Cumberbatch’s character

00:07:38.881 --> 00:07:44.740
says there is no such thing as coincidences,
the universe is rarely so lazy.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:49.880
So I’ll say it is possible that the cracks
in the universe are somehow related to Rusty.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.569
But I think Rusty’s story will be much less
complicated than that.

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:58.500
It’s Danny Pink, Clara and Missy that are
the complicated ones.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:02.050
10 - Zombiestabber asks How do Daleks reproduce?

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:05.699
There are a couple of things they do, primarily
they just clone themselves.

00:08:05.699 --> 00:08:11.159
But over time as their genetic templates degrade
and they assimilate new more advanced beings.

00:08:11.159 --> 00:08:13.640
They update the template.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.970
Changing the template was something that happened
in series 5.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:20.949
The new Dalek Paradigm re-booted their genetic
code to it’s original khaled mutant state.

00:08:20.949 --> 00:08:23.030
Those daleks showed up in a tie-in video game
but they were later retconned out of the series.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.611
The Daleks we met in Asylum are the most current
version, those are the ones that we also saw

00:08:25.611 --> 00:08:26.611
in the christmas special.

00:08:26.611 --> 00:08:29.599
From a reproductive standpoint, they’re
just the same old daleks.

00:08:29.599 --> 00:08:31.180
I think all the converted humans and Oswin
Dalek were one-offs.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.630
Fun fact: If you consider the novels to be
canon, then the time lords also reproduce

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.510
in a similar non-traditional way.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:41.720
They use something called the Loom, a device
developed by Rassilon to resequence Old Time

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:45.010
Lord DNA and weave new Gallifreyans into existence.

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:48.720
I should say that’s how they reproduce on
gallifrey, because not all people on gallifrey

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.720
are time lords.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.950
There’s a theory that the doctor was created
from the re-sequenced DNA of The Other, the

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:59.340
third being that founded the Time Lord society
with Omega and Rassilon.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:04.480
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions,
like I said I’m almost done with my move

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.210
so my video schedule should be back to normal
soon.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:12.830
My next Doctor Who video will post Saturday
morning, that will be my bonus video for favorite

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:17.380
fictional characters brought to life inside
the show.

